  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. The premise that `channel` is no longer read doesn't hold for one consumer.\n\n**`analytics-ingest` still reads `channel` from `OrderPlaced` and requires it:**\n- `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` calls `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`, so a missing `channel` throws `ContractViolationError`.\n- `analytics-ingest/README.md:31` says a missing or unknown `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event.\n- `analytics-ingest/src/ingest.ts:17` writes it to the `orders.channel` column.\n\nIf I removed `channel` from `OrderPlaced`, analytics-ingest would reject every order event once it's deployed.\n\n`billing-service` looks fine. Its test already passes `channel: undefined`, so it doesn't seem to depend on the field.\n\n**Options:**\n1. **Remove it from the order model only.** Drop `channel` from `Order`, `NewOrder`, validation and request parsing, but keep it on the event. That still leaves the event with nothing to fill it from, so this isn't really workable.\n2. **Remove it everywhere, with analytics-ingest changed first.** The analytics team would make `channel` optional or drop it before we ship. Their repo is read-only for me, so that's their change to make.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now.** I'd do this only if you confirm analytics-ingest is already handled or can be broken.\n\nWhich do you want? If you pick 2 or 3, I'll remove `channel` from `src/core/order.ts`, `src/core/events.ts` and `src/api/requestParsing.ts`. I'll also update the tests and helpers and the example in `CLAUDE.md` and `README.md`. After that I'll run `npm test`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run arch`.",
